1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,830
The End

2
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,437
Father, after spending some
time behind these stone walls,

3
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:23,357
I've come to realize how
foolish I was in the past.

4
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:27,857
My desire to steal consumed me,
and from there I lost all control.

5
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:29,720
I am deeply ashamed.

6
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:32,464
It's all thanks to you, Father.

7
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:38,220
And so, may I please have your
assistance in receiving early parole?

8
00:00:38,380 --> 00:00:43,480
Recent studies show that if they
receive the proper training,

9
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:47,440
animals such as dogs and parrots
can learn to read, use fire,

10
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:49,300
and even appreciate art.

11
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:54,497
If that's truly the case, then what's the
difference between humans and animals?

12
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:55,660
Do you know?

13
00:00:56,580 --> 00:00:57,920
Well, yeah, of course.

14
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:00,957
However, I don't see how
that relates to my...

15
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:02,099
Ah, just a moment.

16
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:06,710
Father?

17
00:01:06,793 --> 00:01:07,623
It's done.

18
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:11,500
Have you ever tried this?

19
00:01:11,660 --> 00:01:15,577
The challenge comes after completing the
first cherry with it still in your mouth.

20
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:18,457
Now which tooth must you
use to bite into the second?

21
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:20,437
If you accidentally
bit the first seed that

22
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:22,237
you went through the
trouble of completing,

23
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:23,555
it wouldn't end well.

24
00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:24,690
Uh-huh.

25
00:01:24,773 --> 00:01:27,229
Anyway, sorry, Father,
but about my parole?

26
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:29,510
Hmm.

27
00:01:29,593 --> 00:01:31,040
I think there is a possibility.

28
00:01:31,580 --> 00:01:33,137
Do you really mean it, Father?

29
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:36,897
I will be sure to put in a good
word for you with the committee.

30
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:38,380
Thank you very much!

31
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:47,780
I have taken a liking to
those mischievous hands.

32
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:52,637
Your ill-natured self will never be fixed.

33
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:56,400
But I cannot ignore the
talents you possess.

34
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:59,060
They will be of much use to me.

35
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:02,146
By no means can Jotaro
Stan leave this prison,

36
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:05,280
so I will leave the task
of preventing that to you.

37
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:52,617
I don't want to say no time, let's go.

38
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:56,100
1,2,3 Can we find a way?

39
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:57,500
5, 4, 3

40
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:06,320
We're coming low

41
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:25,260
time I don't stop beating,

42
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:29,580
don't stop beating, don't
stop beating, I'm up!

43
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:45,250
What?

44
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:48,772
The hell do you mean you had
FF hide it somewhere for you?

45
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:53,117
After all that effort it took to get
it, it's got your dad's stand on it.

46
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,259
Sure, that's okay.

47
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:55,777
Do you even know where it is?

48
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:56,937
I mean, they're still in...

49
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:58,320
This place is so fun!

50
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:00,637
Compared to the swamp, it's lovely.

51
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:01,550
Seriously?

52
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:04,917
We should do what
they're doing over there.

53
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,412
I think it's called playing catch, right?

54
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:09,960
Look, I trust FF.

55
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:14,857
And as far as we know, Pale Snake
has no clue our new friend's alive.

56
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:16,200
It's safer this way.

57
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:18,031
Yeah, guess you're right.

58
00:04:19,460 --> 00:04:20,637
But look at it like this,

59
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:24,077
wouldn't it be even better to send
it to the people holding your dad?

60
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:24,990
It would.

61
00:04:25,073 --> 00:04:25,903
Thing is,

62
00:04:25,986 --> 00:04:28,857
I tried to escape so my phone
and visitor privileges are gone,

63
00:04:28,940 --> 00:04:32,234
and I still haven't come up
with a plan to carry it out.

64
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:36,517
Hey, you fugly ho!

65
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:38,482
Take that out of your mouth now!

66
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:39,570
Huh?

67
00:04:39,653 --> 00:04:40,877
What did you just say to me?

68
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:43,617
I replenish my thirst
and you hurl insults?

69
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:45,000
Put the cup down now!

70
00:04:45,220 --> 00:04:47,337
They're on the bench where
you found it, immediately!

71
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:50,717
If it's that important to you, you
shouldn't leave it sitting around,

72
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:52,682
especially in a place like this.

73
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:57,620
Just ignore her!

74
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:59,077
We'll go get you more water!

75
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:01,160
It's okay, FF, don't make a scene!

76
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:06,790
Please!

77
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:17,520
Give it here! Huh?

78
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:19,480
Well, I guess it's okay.

79
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:22,340
There's actually more here now. Lucky me!

80
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,080
All right.

81
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:31,060
Let's throw the ball around, yeah? What?

82
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:32,980
Good grief.

83
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:35,476
You've never thrown a ball, have you?

84
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:37,350
Uh-oh.

85
00:05:45,820 --> 00:05:47,520
Nah, pull your hips back in.

86
00:05:47,780 --> 00:05:48,760
A little more.

87
00:05:51,580 --> 00:05:53,660
There you go, looking good, right?

88
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:56,995
Jolene, did you know?

89
00:05:57,780 --> 00:06:00,320
We've gone back and
forth 86 times already.

90
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,088
We haven't dropped it once!

91
00:06:02,180 --> 00:06:03,709
Think we'll hit a hundred?

92
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:07,260
A hundred dollars says you won't. Huh?

93
00:06:08,980 --> 00:06:10,400
Will you take that bet?

94
00:06:11,220 --> 00:06:12,557
Sorry, but who are you?

95
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:14,052
And what are you saying?

96
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:19,160
My name is Mirashon, and
FE26789 is my prisoner number.

97
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:21,357
I'm saying you won't catch the ball.

98
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:22,897
I'm willing to bet a hundred dollars!

99
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:24,037
that your little game of catch?

100
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:26,238
will end before you reach a hundred.

101
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:28,497
Don't you think this is
coming out of nowhere?

102
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:29,992
What do you really want?

103
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:31,771
Just trying to kill time.

104
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:39,230
Let's do it!

105
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:41,120
It's only 13 more passes!

106
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:42,928
Hey, not another word, you!

107
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:45,210
Regardless,

108
00:06:45,293 --> 00:06:49,197
I don't have anywhere near that amount of
money on me, so it won't be much of a bet.

109
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:51,217
Well, it doesn't have
to be money, you know.

110
00:06:51,300 --> 00:06:56,065
I'll take drugs, cigarettes, chewing gum,
some phone time, hell, even a vibrator.

111
00:06:56,380 --> 00:06:58,157
Anything with a bit of value will do.

112
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,860
I'll be frank with you.

113
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:02,380
I don't really do bets, so get lost.

114
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:04,378
Wait just a second.

115
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:05,597
Come on, Jolene.

116
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:07,445
You should go along with this.

117
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:11,938
We've got some crazy luck, and
whatever you don't have, I'll lend you.

118
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:15,877
FF sucks at throwing, but they've
managed to do it 87 times.

119
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:16,800
We can win.

120
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:18,937
There's more to it than that.

121
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:21,902
Yeah, it might be a trap
set by Palesnake, right?

122
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:23,908
But I know that Mira shown.

123
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:26,021
We're on the same floor together.

124
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:30,177
She's a stupid gambler that ruined
her life committing small robberies.

125
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:31,731
Think about it for a sec.

126
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:34,997
When you're finally able to
use the phones and get visits,

127
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:39,437
you're definitely going to wish you had
this money to buy your place in line.

128
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:42,657
Hey, are you in or are
you not? Count me in!

129
00:07:42,740 --> 00:07:43,857
I want to do it for sure!

130
00:07:43,940 --> 00:07:45,058
We can totally win!

131
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:48,800
Okay, but do you even have $100 on you?

132
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:55,370
We'll play,

133
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:59,097
but conditions are if you raise your voice
or move even one step from that spot,

134
00:07:59,180 --> 00:08:00,197
the bet is called off.

135
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:01,110
Got it?

136
00:08:01,193 --> 00:08:03,373
So the game has already begun then, huh?

137
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:05,677
But it won't be fair
if the distance is too

138
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:08,397
close or if you hold on
to the ball for too long.

139
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:11,362
More than three meters
apart, within ten seconds.

140
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:13,190
Okay.

141
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:17,497
All right, let's get this thing started!

142
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:19,462
Just calm down before you throw.

143
00:08:19,820 --> 00:08:22,291
You've got ten seconds, so take your time.

144
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:24,840
And that makes 89.

145
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:28,400
Now there's only 11 more to go.

146
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:30,397
You little...

147
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:34,040
Get those sticky fingers the
hell away from my water! Hey!

148
00:08:37,060 --> 00:08:38,220
Way too close.

149
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:39,955
Concentrate, damn it!

150
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,300
That's not it!

151
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:43,173
She's the problem here!

152
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:45,142
What is she doing near my water?

153
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:47,100
I'm just spectating quietly.

154
00:08:47,660 --> 00:08:49,840
Well, do it away from my cup or else!

155
00:08:50,580 --> 00:08:51,540
Fine, whatever.

156
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:55,020
Clock's ticking. Go,
Ephef! Throw the ball!

157
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,200
Screw this girl!

158
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:57,360
She's bugging me!

159
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:59,597
I'll hold your water, now throw the ball!

160
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:00,510
One second.

161
00:09:00,593 --> 00:09:01,580
Throw it! Shit!

162
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:04,470
Idiot!

163
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:10,050
Joey!

164
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:15,634
That was close, but you pulled through.

165
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:16,630
I'm sorry.

166
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:18,154
I panicked back there.

167
00:09:19,520 --> 00:09:21,680
Be more careful next time, FF.

168
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:23,900
Yeah, right. I'm fine now.

169
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:27,070
Here we go!

170
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:29,180
That was a hundred times! Okay.

171
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:33,397
With the way I'm feeling, a hundred
more times sounds like a breeze, too!

172
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:35,397
It was an easy win like I thought.

173
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:37,157
Now fork over the hundred dollars.

174
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:38,070
No.

175
00:09:38,153 --> 00:09:39,997
You were betting with FF
earlier, too, weren't you?

176
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,717
So doesn't that mean it
should be two hundred?

177
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:42,630
Yeah, true.

178
00:09:42,713 --> 00:09:44,237
It definitely should be two hundred.

179
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:45,908
Hurry up and give it to me.

180
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:50,316
I've got a grand on you not
being able to do it again.

181
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:54,749
What, did you not hear me?

182
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:56,921
I'm telling you my bet is $1,000.

183
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,760
Are you for real?

184
00:09:58,940 --> 00:10:00,817
Do you even have that kind of cash?

185
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:01,730
Of course.

186
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:03,252
But like I said earlier,

187
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:06,597
anything with value will
do the trick just the same.

188
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:09,520
The rules remain unchanged
as well. Sound good?

189
00:10:10,940 --> 00:10:12,800
No, we're done with your games.

190
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:16,053
We might have just won.

191
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:19,000
But honestly, I don't like you one bit.

192
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:22,637
So if you want to bet,
take it somewhere else.

193
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:23,897
I'll go instead of her.

194
00:10:23,980 --> 00:10:25,980
Well, okay. Abs, here!

195
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:27,657
Give me the bowling glove!

196
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:28,620
On it! Irvis!

197
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:33,077
Jolene, I don't like this
chick all that much either.

198
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:35,631
Or the way she's oddly fixated on betting.

199
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:41,260
But still, if it's going to be
$1,200 including the earlier bet,

200
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:43,457
there's no way we can pass this up.

201
00:10:43,540 --> 00:10:44,877
You might want to be careful.

202
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:49,337
Like the rules of the last game, this
one began the moment you decided to play.

203
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:51,797
You've less than 10 seconds. Throw it!

204
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:52,821
I'm in your way!

205
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,420
It's another easy victory!

206
00:11:02,940 --> 00:11:03,770
30!

207
00:11:05,020 --> 00:11:05,850
31!

208
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:07,710
32!

209
00:11:08,700 --> 00:11:09,530
Nice!

210
00:11:09,613 --> 00:11:10,638
Next we'll be a 33!

211
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:12,750
Huh?

212
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:13,800
That's enough!

213
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:15,609
Put away the gear already!

214
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:18,000
Today's exercise period is over!

215
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:21,240
Five seconds.

216
00:11:23,060 --> 00:11:23,890
F's catch!

217
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,310
33!

218
00:11:25,500 --> 00:11:26,757
The hell's your damage?

219
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:29,597
We're not gonna have ourselves
a problem here, are we?

220
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:30,510
Hey, you!

221
00:11:30,593 --> 00:11:31,637
We're calling this bed off!

222
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:32,550
It's done!

223
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:34,397
Okay, here's a thought for you.

224
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:36,517
Let's suppose for a moment now that a

225
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:39,337
meteorite fell from the
heavens out of nowhere.

226
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:40,440
Sure, it's wild,

227
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:44,357
but you'd probably think that the game
should be called off, like it's just over.

228
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:46,317
You'd say it's the Meteor's fault.

229
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:49,400
And not to convince me,
mind you, but yourselves.

230
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:52,226
But are you sure that's okay?

231
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:55,757
Don't you think you two might
have run out of exercise time?

232
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:59,997
Because you were taking your sweet time
and deliberately throwing the ball slowly?

233
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:02,277
Take a good look into
your heart and you'll see.

234
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:05,097
If it's telling you you didn't break
any rules, there's no need to worry.

235
00:12:05,180 --> 00:12:09,180
By all means, if you're innocent,
you can stop the game at any time.

236
00:12:09,580 --> 00:12:10,410
Fuck you!

237
00:12:10,493 --> 00:12:11,323
That's it, Armas!

238
00:12:11,406 --> 00:12:14,085
Be prepared to be sent
to solitary confinement!

239
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:17,930
Please, Mr.

240
00:12:18,013 --> 00:12:19,254
Guard, just this once.

241
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:20,230
Five minutes.

242
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:21,479
No, three will do.

243
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:24,150
Two minutes.

244
00:12:24,260 --> 00:12:26,157
I'm gonna go make my rounds over here.

245
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:27,500
Fs, now! Hurry up!

246
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:31,300
But a measly $100 will only go so far.

247
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:33,322
I'd say it only covers the ball.

248
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:37,040
I'll be taking that
glove. Give it her! What?

249
00:12:41,060 --> 00:12:41,890
Dammit!

250
00:12:46,220 --> 00:12:47,160
Ah, shit!

251
00:12:49,580 --> 00:12:53,874
But in case something like this might
happen, I'd put a sticker on there.

252
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:00,340
Hermes, no!

253
00:13:05,560 --> 00:13:06,880
Let's keep going.

254
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:12,740
I'm merely a spectator here.

255
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:16,460
I won't move a muscle or even think.

256
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:19,661
But still, though I can't
prove what she just did.

257
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:25,320
On the inside, Ermes knows
exactly what happened.

258
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:28,360
There's no denying it.

259
00:13:28,620 --> 00:13:30,973
Your bestie just broke one of the rules.

260
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:38,000
I know because the debt collector, Mary
Lynn Manson, has appeared before us.

261
00:13:42,880 --> 00:13:44,860
Hermes, hey! Watch yourself!

262
00:13:45,060 --> 00:13:46,178
She's a stand user!

263
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:54,620
No matter where you hide it
away or what the item is,

264
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:58,380
it takes absolutely everything
and leaves nothing behind.

265
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:02,500
This is still not enough.

266
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:04,190
Sticker!

267
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:07,420
Game over.

268
00:14:14,340 --> 00:14:15,170
Hermes!

269
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:26,530
Hermes!

270
00:14:26,613 --> 00:14:29,297
If you sold this liver I'm
holding on the Black Market,

271
00:14:29,380 --> 00:14:33,060
It would make up for the
remaining $590 that you owe.

272
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:35,720
Piss off! Oh, shit!

273
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:42,420
I am the shadow that lies
deep within Hermes' heart.

274
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:45,657
The two of you cannot
possibly land an attack on me.

275
00:14:45,740 --> 00:14:47,597
Hermes has broken the
rules you established,

276
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:50,151
and has therefore lost the bet on her own.

277
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:53,157
I came to collect the debt
weighing on her shoulders.

278
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:55,737
Or are there any other
precious items she may have?

279
00:14:55,820 --> 00:14:59,467
If so, I can exchange this liver
for something of equal value.

280
00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:02,680
This bet still isn't over yet. What?

281
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:05,717
We'll catch the ball a thousand times.

282
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:09,557
And if we succeed, you'll give
back everything you took from her.

283
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:12,300
And then just leave us
the hell alone. Okay.

284
00:15:12,860 --> 00:15:15,037
However, I'm sure you're
aware of how this goes.

285
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:17,473
You must offer something of equal value.

286
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:19,320
Yeah, I know. Excellent.

287
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:21,934
With the rules set, the game has begun.

288
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:23,330
See you later.

289
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:25,720
Esa, here!

290
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:30,440
J-Jolene!

291
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:33,460
Ermes, you're not the one at fault here.

292
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:39,184
Since Miraschon is a stand user, there's
a high chance that Palesnake is involved.

293
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:42,437
If that's the case, then they're
aiming for my dad's disc.

294
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:44,461
That's what the Collector is for.

295
00:15:44,560 --> 00:15:45,440
There you go.

296
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:48,358
Another reason not to take this bet.

297
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:52,297
You got dragged into this shit
fest because of my family drama.

298
00:15:52,380 --> 00:15:54,260
I can't let you die for me.

299
00:15:54,780 --> 00:15:56,957
But how the hell are we
going to pull this off?

300
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:59,097
We're talking about a
thousand throws in a row.

301
00:15:59,180 --> 00:16:01,637
And that thing earlier
was basically invincible.

302
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:03,400
Yeah, that's exactly why.

303
00:16:03,660 --> 00:16:07,131
We're going to chase down
Miroshon and attack her directly.

304
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:12,016
That greedy stand of hers may be
invincible, but her body is fair game.

305
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:15,367
That's why she's putting
distance between us.

306
00:16:16,460 --> 00:16:17,290
Let's go!

307
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:27,310
You see her?

308
00:16:27,393 --> 00:16:29,157
I'm sure I saw her come in here.

309
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:30,817
That door on the other side of the room.

310
00:16:30,900 --> 00:16:32,665
She must have left from there.

311
00:16:34,180 --> 00:16:35,180
Pass into you.

312
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:37,930
Jolene.

313
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:38,970
Wait!

314
00:16:39,053 --> 00:16:39,883
Don't throw!

315
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:43,830
Seriously!

316
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:45,070
Shut up!

317
00:16:45,153 --> 00:16:45,983
As I threw the ball.

318
00:16:46,066 --> 00:16:46,896
Yeah!

319
00:16:46,979 --> 00:16:47,809
But where?

320
00:16:47,892 --> 00:16:48,722
I can't see a damn thing.

321
00:16:48,805 --> 00:16:49,635
Don't move!

322
00:16:49,718 --> 00:16:50,548
It'll probably hit your body.

323
00:16:57,560 --> 00:16:58,390
It's okay!

324
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:01,260
I got the ball! That's great, FF!

325
00:17:01,500 --> 00:17:03,637
Now let's just stay calm
and keep the ball moving!

326
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:04,550
Over here!

327
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:06,820
Where the hell is here? Hurry!

328
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:09,940
It's already over.

329
00:17:11,060 --> 00:17:12,080
I'm right here!

330
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:14,820
Now I'm angry!

331
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,320
You're fighting a fool.

332
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:27,817
I heard a voice come from
somewhere over there.

333
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:30,606
So I fired randomly in
that general direction.

334
00:17:32,140 --> 00:17:32,980
Damn it.

335
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:34,807
What the fuck is that thing?

336
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:40,200
We are now nearing lockdown time.

337
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:42,877
All prisoners must return
to their cells immediately

338
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:45,725
and remain standing until
the roll call begins.

339
00:17:45,900 --> 00:17:48,606
I repeat, the roll call
will commence shortly.

340
00:17:52,020 --> 00:17:53,380
Look, she ran that way!

341
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,640
How unfortunate for you.

342
00:18:05,940 --> 00:18:07,577
There's nowhere left to run.

343
00:18:07,660 --> 00:18:11,797
And now that I know you're a fellow
stand user, I won't need to hold back.

344
00:18:11,880 --> 00:18:13,080
Hey, wait a second.

345
00:18:13,620 --> 00:18:15,480
Take the money, and deliver.

346
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:17,077
Here, it's all yours!

347
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:19,101
That's not the only thing I want.

348
00:18:19,220 --> 00:18:23,279
For starters, I want to know who in
this prison gave you stand power.

349
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:27,160
It was Palesnake, right? Don't lie.

350
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:29,280
Tell me who they really are.

351
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:31,497
What are you talking about?

352
00:18:31,580 --> 00:18:33,757
You sure you got time to be playing dumb?

353
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:35,075
You gotta believe me!

354
00:18:35,180 --> 00:18:36,417
I don't know who that is!

355
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:38,618
All I wanted to do was go on parole!

356
00:18:44,700 --> 00:18:45,660
This is...

357
00:18:46,780 --> 00:18:47,740
An elevator.

358
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:50,405
One that transports our meals.

359
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:52,320
How much longer now?

360
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:53,600
Six seconds?

361
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:55,320
Or is it five?

362
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:56,930
No!

363
00:18:57,520 --> 00:18:58,350
Julian!

364
00:19:04,460 --> 00:19:05,680
Two more.

365
00:19:07,520 --> 00:19:08,780
FF, the ball!

366
00:19:09,060 --> 00:19:10,680
Come on, FF, throw it here!

367
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:14,710
Shit!

368
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:19,470
Nice job.

369
00:19:19,620 --> 00:19:21,149
Now what are you gonna do?

370
00:19:22,020 --> 00:19:23,785
You've got eight more seconds.

371
00:19:24,380 --> 00:19:25,210
Seven.

372
00:19:25,940 --> 00:19:26,770
Six.

373
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:31,800
Catch him now!

374
00:19:39,020 --> 00:19:40,880
This is what you wanted.

375
00:19:41,060 --> 00:19:42,648
Ain't that right, Mirachon?

376
00:19:43,480 --> 00:19:47,117
Taking care of easy and convenient
favors like this is nothing for me.

377
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:48,360
Need anything else?

378
00:19:48,540 --> 00:19:49,716
Just give me a call.

379
00:19:58,680 --> 00:20:00,480
Try catching the ball now!

380
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:03,040
Oh, you can't anymore, can you?

381
00:20:03,540 --> 00:20:05,220
This game of catch is over!

382
00:20:05,940 --> 00:20:08,080
You're dead, Jolyne Keicho!

383
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:12,852
Mary Lynn Manson will always
come to collect what is owed!

384
00:20:13,020 --> 00:20:15,200
No matter where they may be hidden.

385
00:20:15,940 --> 00:20:18,980
Even if you are unaware,
Mary Lynn will know!

386
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:20,550
Jolene!

387
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:23,649
First, I'll take your
most expensive organ.

388
00:20:23,860 --> 00:20:27,117
And to cover the remainder, I'll
take your most precious possession.

389
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:29,000
Your father's stand disc.

390
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,220
As for where to find it...

391
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:38,276
That psychotic brat FF has had it
behind them since the very beginning!

392
00:20:39,100 --> 00:20:40,140
I won!

393
00:20:40,760 --> 00:20:43,637
Now I've got your organ and your disc!

394
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:45,820
It all belongs to me!

395
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:52,520
This little game of
catch is far from over.

396
00:20:57,060 --> 00:20:58,077
But how?

397
00:20:58,160 --> 00:20:59,000
The ball?

398
00:21:12,260 --> 00:21:13,090
Impossible.

399
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:18,037
Cheater no, I never actually specified
the person I'd be playing catch with.

400
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:20,540
The guard counts too?

401
00:21:28,360 --> 00:21:30,800
Seems like the collector also improves.

402
00:21:32,460 --> 00:21:37,357
Now that we have 800 more
balls to catch or was it 900?

403
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:39,380
You know what? Screw it!

404
00:22:08,100 --> 00:22:10,597
I'm gonna get my dad's
disc out of this prison.

405
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:14,120
And that includes the one
Palesnake's holding on to.

406
00:22:14,560 --> 00:22:15,640
Just watch.

407
00:22:26,700 --> 00:22:30,460
Although you think I cope

408
00:22:31,540 --> 00:22:35,657
My head is filled with hope

409
00:22:35,740 --> 00:22:40,017
Of some place

410
00:22:40,100 --> 00:22:43,760
other than here

411
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:50,160
Although you think I smile

412
00:22:51,780 --> 00:22:55,220
Inside and all the while

413
00:22:57,020 --> 00:23:03,400
I'm wondering about my destiny?

414
00:23:05,940 --> 00:23:07,877
I'm thinking

415
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:13,557
about all the

416
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:18,417
things I'd like

417
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:24,440
to do in my life.

418
00:23:25,940 --> 00:23:29,320
I'm a dreamer.

419
00:23:30,140 --> 00:23:34,420
A distant dreamer.

420
00:23:36,340 --> 00:23:39,680
Dreaming far away.

421
00:23:41,740 --> 00:23:44,540
From today!

422
00:23:54,620 --> 00:23:55,450
Thank you.

423
00:24:31,620 --> 00:24:33,060
Thank you.
